## 10. What not to repeat unnecessarily

* Do not reinstall Ryu or OVS every time you start a lab session.

* Do not downgrade Eventlet to `0.30.2` on this Python 3.10 environment.

* Do not restart OVS or change system networking while the cluster is running unless we have diagnosed a specific problem.

* Do not attach Kubernetes/Calico interfaces to `br-ryu-test`.

* Do not treat userspace `netdev` benchmark results as equivalent to kernel-datapath OVS performance.

Your current verified milestone is: Ryu 4.34 running in the virtual environment, OVS 2.17.12 using `netdev`, and `br-ryu-test` connected to Ryu over OpenFlow 1.3. That establishes the control connection; full multi-switch packet forwarding and predictive rerouting are still future steps.

